# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust for your network.
#
# Defaults (docker-compose.yml): images are pulled from their canonical
# registries (Docker Hub, gcr.io, Docker Hub's nvidia/dcgm-exporter).
#
# On a restricted network (e.g. mainland China), configure a registry mirror
# in Docker Desktop -> Settings -> Docker Engine, for example:
#
#   "registry-mirrors": ["https://docker.m.daocloud.io"]
#
# Docker Hub images (prom/prometheus, grafana/grafana, oliver006/redis_exporter,
# nvidia/dcgm-exporter) then pull through the mirror. gcr.io is NOT covered by
# registry-mirrors, so override the cAdvisor image with a mirror prefix:

## China mirror overrides
# CADVISOR_IMAGE=docker.m.daocloud.io/gcr.io/cadvisor/cadvisor:latest
# PROMETHEUS_IMAGE=docker.m.daocloud.io/prom/prometheus:latest
# GRAFANA_IMAGE=docker.m.daocloud.io/grafana/grafana:latest
# REDIS_EXPORTER_IMAGE=docker.m.daocloud.io/oliver006/redis_exporter:latest
# DCGM_EXPORTER_IMAGE=docker.m.daocloud.io/nvidia/dcgm-exporter:3.3.7-3.5.0

## Alternative DCGM exporter sources (pick the tag that exists for your driver):
# DCGM_EXPORTER_IMAGE=nvcr.io/nvidia/k8s/dcgm-exporter:3.3.7-3.5.0
# DCGM_EXPORTER_IMAGE=docker.m.daocloud.io/nvcr.io/nvidia/k8s/dcgm-exporter:3.3.7-3.5.0
